      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "Since we know that the triangle is a right triangle, we can use our knowledge of basic triangle properties to help us solve the problem.\n\nProperty 1: Opposite sides opposite each other in a right triangle are perpendicular to each other.\nProperty 2: The hypotenuse (the side that is opposite the right angle) is the longest side in a right triangle.\n\nSince the length of the hypotenuse in a right triangle that is a decreasing sum of the other two sides, we can conclude that the hypotenuse of our right triangle is 8 cm long, because 6+8=14 and 14 is less than 16. \nUsing another property of right triangles, we know that the hypotenuse is the longest side, and all other sides are always shorter than the hypotenuse.\n\nThus, the two sides adjacent to the hypotenuse must be:\n\nsqrt(8^2-6^2)=sqrt(64-36)=sqrt(28)=5.292 cm \nSince we previously said that all other sides in a right triangle are always shorter than the hypotenuse. We must get closer to establishing a value for the side of length 5.28 for a short side.\n\nSince the obtained value is the shortest possible side length, we're done. \nTherefore, the side of length 5.28cm is the smallest possible side of a right triangle with side lengths of sides 6cm, 8cm and is opposite the right angle.\n\n\\boxed{5.28}",
